    "result_text": "The full suite (AcceptanceTest, 2 tests) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `locality` derivation from the owner's city using the fixed city-to-region table.\n\n**Approach \u2014 minimal structural impact (2 files):** `locality` is a derived, read-only field on the generated `OwnerDto`, produced the same way the codebase already produces `membershipTier` \u2014 an inline MapStruct expression. No entity, function class, or endpoint YAML changes were needed.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `locality` schema property to the Owner schema (read-only string, documented mapping), which generates the DTO field.\n2. `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added one `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = ...)` line to `toOwnerDto`, mapping `Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`, else `UNKNOWN`.\n\nThe edited `toOwnerDto` is an abstract interface method (CC 1) in a small interface, so the added complexity is confined to a single low-context annotation line. Both new acceptance tests (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, unknown city\u2192`UNKNOWN`) and the full suite pass.",
